  \uc0\u9888 \u65039   Two corrections to my earlier runbook\
\
  Correction 1 \'97 the kill hostname is NOT agent-01.\
  The agent polls /api/response/pending?hostname=<os.Hostname()>, but events are\
  stored under the cert CN agent-01. These are different strings. The kill command\
  must be queued under the value real_agent actually polls with \'97 its OS hostname.\
  Since the curl runs on the same box, use $(hostname) so it always matches:\
\
  curl -X POST localhost:8080/api/response/kill \\\
    -d "\{\\"hostname\\":\\"$(hostname)\\",\\"pid\\":1201,\\"issued_by\\":\\"manager\\"\}"\
\
  (If you hardcode agent-01, the poll returns nothing and the kill silently never\
  executes \'97 exactly the trap to avoid mid-demo.)\
\
  Correction 2 \'97 the kill result shows in the terminal, NOT Grafana.\
  There's no dashboard panel for response_commands. Within \uc0\u8804 10s of the curl, the\
  real_agent terminal prints:\
  [\uc0\u55357 \u57057 \u65039   MOCK DEFENSE] Terminated malicious PID: 1201\
  executed kill command id=... pid=1201\
  and the command flips PENDING\uc0\u8594 EXECUTED in the DB. To show that flip, either\
  re-run the curl-GET or query the table:\
  curl "localhost:8080/api/response/pending?hostname=$(hostname)"   # empty after \
  execution\
\
  ---\
  Bottom line\
\
  The detect\uc0\u8594 alert\u8594 respond loop works end-to-end. Two narration notes for your\
  manager: identity comes from the mTLS cert (agent-01) for telemetry, and the\
  response result is in the agent log (the mock-defense line is actually a nice\
  visual).\
\
